<title>JAPAN: NTT says to take 35 pct stake in Sri Lanka Telecom.</title>
<headline>NTT says to take 35 pct stake in Sri Lanka Telecom.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp on Monday confirmed recent newspaper reports that it would acquire a 35 percent stake in Sri Lanka Telecom Ltd for $225 million.</p>
<p>An NTT spokesman said the investment would be formerly announced by the Sri Lanka government shortly.  </p>
<p>NTT is considering sending managers and engineers to work at Sri Lanka Telecom, he said.</p>
<p>The Sri Lankan government will hold the remaining 65 percent stake in the company, the NTT spokesman said.</p>
</text>
